#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# difference_root_reduce

#% text
# `difference_root_reduce(lhs == rhs, n)` decides an identity between sequences of the integer n: `true` when it holds, `false` when it fails.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The two sides are compared exactly at n = 0, 1, ..., 40. For holonomic sides (Fibonacci and Lucas numbers, polynomials, factorials, binomials, ...) whose difference satisfies a recurrence of order below that, agreement on these terms proves the identity.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
difference_root_reduce(fibonacci(n + 1)*fibonacci(n - 1) - fibonacci(n)^2 == (-1)^n, n)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
difference_root_reduce(fibonacci(2*n) == fibonacci(n)*lucas_l(n), n)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
difference_root_reduce(fibonacci(n + 1) == (fibonacci(n) + lucas_l(n))/2, n)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
difference_root_reduce(fibonacci(n) == n, n)
#% output
#= false

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `difference_root`, `fibonacci`, `lucas_l`
